  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "80946e29-2bdf-4cce-81a4-2cbbd89e30d5",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1248,
        -160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 992,
        "content": "## Client Project Radar — The Ambiguity Gate\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow captures client project updates from Telegram, uses Gemini to extract the update details and match them against an active client roster, then routes ambiguous matches back to the user for clarification. Clear updates are normalized, appended to Notion, optionally archive Telegram attachments to Google Drive, logged in Google Sheets, and confirmed back in Telegram. A separate daily schedule gathers upcoming Google Calendar events and recent audit-log activity, summarizes them with Gemini, and sends a one-message Telegram digest.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure Telegram credentials for the trigger and message-sending nodes, including the chat IDs used for confirmations, ambiguity questions, failure alerts, and daily digests.\n- Connect Google Gemini credentials for the three LLM chains and verify the structured output parsers match the expected schemas.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and set the active-client roster sheet plus the audit/read-log sheet ranges and columns.\n- Connect Notion credentials and configure the target page or database used by the timeline append step.\n- Connect Google Drive credentials and choose the folder where Telegram attachments should be archived.\n- Connect Google Calendar credentials and select the calendar queried for the next seven days.\n- Confirm the daily schedule trigger time zone and 08:00 run time.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the Gemini prompts and parser schemas for your preferred update fields, client-matching confidence threshold, ambiguity wording, audit-log columns, attachment folder structure, and daily brief format."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "030e4edf-e6b8-484f-b30f-896dc6dcf6ed",
